19DEC2024 @hanoihantrakul
Implementation notes:

The Vocos is a pretrained model which operates on mono mel spectrograms at 24khz.

There are 2 key implementation items:

- Vocos has a default hop_size=256, which at 24khz means the mel_feature_rate=93.75
This is different from our tokenizer which has hop_size=240, which at 24khz means the mel_feature_rate=100
To solve this problem, I simply task the decoder with reconstructing the mel at 93.75Hz and then zero padding
to what it should have been 100hz. Essentially the FrozenUMM-Mel-Decoder is decoding a "truncated mel spectrogram".
Obviously the proper way to fix this is to completely retrain Vocos with a hop_size=240 but I just don't have
time for this task with only 2 weeks left at the company.

- Vocos operates on mono signals, so to generate stereo signals I invert the left and right mel channel separately.